# Flags Test (Star and Priority)

Tests star flag (+) and priority flags (!, !!, !!!).


## Star Flag

[ ] + Important task with star flag
[ ] + Another starred task
    [ ] + Nested starred task


## Priority Flags

[ ] ! Priority level 1 (high)
[ ] !! Priority level 2 (higher)
[ ] !!! Priority level 3 (highest)
[ ] !!!! Priority level 4+ (treated as level 3)
[ ] !!!!!! Many exclamation marks (treated as level 3)


## Combined with Task States

[@] + In-progress starred task
[x] + Completed starred task
[w] ! Waiting high-priority task
[~] !! Cancelled high-priority task


## Nested Priority Tasks

[ ] ! Parent high-priority task
    [ ] !! Child higher-priority task
        [ ] !!! Grandchild highest-priority task


## Invalid Flag Examples (should be treated as normal text)

[ ] +No space after flag - invalid
[ ] !No space after flag - invalid
[ ] !!No space - invalid


## Mixed Flags and Comments

[ ] + Starred task with comment
    /// This task is very important
[ ] !!! Highest priority task
    This task must be completed first.
    It has critical dependencies.


## Flags on Single-Line Comments

/// + Starred single-line comment
/// ! Priority 1 single-line comment
/// !! Priority 2 single-line comment
/// !!! Priority 3 single-line comment
[ ] Task with flagged notes
    /// + A starred note under a task
    /// !! A high priority note under a task
/// +No space after the flag - invalid (normal comment text)


## Star and Priority Together (either order)

Both flags get their own face. The commands (C-c C-s, C-c C-f 1/2/3) write the star first and keep the other flag.

[ ] + ! Star and priority 1
[ ] ! + Priority 1 and star (same meaning)
[ ] + !!! Star and priority 3
[ ] !!! + Priority 3 and star
[ ] ++ Not a flag: two stars are plain text
[ ] + + Only the first star is a flag
